 "notes": "Libretto by Lorenzo Da Ponte (1790). Words follow the Peters engraving's spelling and punctuation: degl' occhi as two words and a voi davanti, where the libretto has o a voi davanti. Guglielmo's first word is printed babara, a misprint for barbara; the word text keeps the print's letters so it lines up with the notes, and its IPA and meaning are those of barbara. Don Alfonso's miei and Fiordiligi's dovrei are sung in more syllables than they are spelt, and their IPA follows the score. IPA, word meanings and translations come from the app's reviewed Così libretto drafts (L30, IPA checked against Castel). IPA follows sung Italian conventions: stressed syllable marked, elisions (two words on one note in the score) joined with ‿, open e/o as ɛ/ɔ. Translation literal, for meaning.",
